integ5 0089 = patches/glue5/0074-glm-decode-hc-partial-split.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

glm cuda: hc_pre's decode dots over more blocks (T3 candidate 9, glue5; exact, switchable)

tf_glm_hc_partial8 (decode rows < 64) makes a row's 16 K blocks' 24 mixing dots and squares sum in 16 blocks of
1,024 threads, each block loading all 24 fn rows of its K block (48 KB): latency-bound at one row (prof5: 2.7 us x 90
a plain step, 16 of 188 SMs busy).
- glm_glue_hc.cuh: tf_glm_hc_partial8_o1 / _o2 / _o4 / _o8 (glm_hcp::partial_split<M>): block (row, K block, z) of
  128 M threads makes dots z M .. z M + M - 1, each (dot, step) on one 16-lane half-warp with tf_glm_hc_partial8's
  lanes, loads, fma chain, butterfly and step sum from 0.0f; block z = 24 / M makes the squares sum with
  tf_glm_hc_partial8's group-0 threads and order. tf_glm_hc_partial8 itself is untouched (the SASS of every existing
  glm_glue kernel unchanged).
- cuda_glue.hcPre: decode rows take the variant Set.hc_part's steps give for their rows (glue.partSplit; grid z
  24 / M + 1, 128 M threads); past the last step, tf_glm_hc_partial8. TF_GLM_HC_PART (read once at load, local to
  the rank): unset/1/on the default steps, 2:16 (M 2 up to 16 rows, tf_glm_hc_partial8 above: bench_hcpart's
  measured best, o2 winning at 1-16 rows and partial8 from 32), 0/off none, or up to four "M:rows" steps
  ("1:4,8:32"); a bad value fails the load. Same arguments, same scratch; prompt rows (>= 64) unchanged.
- Measured (GPU0 400 W, graph-timed, cold weights, us a call): partial8 -> o2 2.40 -> 1.69 at 1 row, 2.40 -> 1.74
  at 4, 2.58 -> 2.52 at 8, 4.45 -> 4.10 at 16; at 32 rows partial8 7.07 against o2 8.70 (and o8 12.24).
- Exact: every partial byte against tf_glm_hc_partial8 (glue5/bench_hcpart.cu: rows 1-63, random, signed-zero and
  wide-range inputs).

